<Project
    title={frontmatter.title}
    subtitle=""
    description=`<p>
        Set within the historic shell of St. Mary's Church, this adaptive reuse
        project blurs the boundaries between residence and commerce. A large plaza
        welcomes visitors with park-like features, anchoring a spatial sequence
        that unfolds across four distinct programs: a ground-floor gathering space
        for markets and concerts, basement workshops for artists and lecturers,
        upper-level galleries for public art, and a rooftop garden for cultivation
        and community.
    </p>
    <br />
    <p>
        Designed to foster a self-sustaining ecosystem, the building invites
        low-income residents to live, work, and play within a shared environment.
        Circulation weaves vertically through the core, echoing the branching
        complexity of nature and encouraging interaction across levels. Apartment
        units integrate old and new structures, balancing privacy with access to
        communal courtyards and shared spaces. The architecture becomes a
        framework for unity—where talent, greenery, and public life converge.
    </p>`
